# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-plugin-spec-and-manual — document the plug-in system (spec, user manual, man page, release notes)
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: doc
#+DEPENDS: alfe-plugin-model
#+BRANCH: master

* Context

Part of the epic =alfe-plugin-model=. Per AGENTS.md ("Documentation
Synchronisation"): a user-visible feature is documented in the user manual
of the tool concerned *before its issue is closed*, and a spec change is
reviewed against code, user manual and man page. The design comes first
(pjb, 2026-09-21: "1 reorganise the issues, 2 design the plug-ins, 3
document, 4 implement, 5 the two first plug-ins").

* Proposal

- =documentation/alfe--specifications.org=: a new chapter "Plug-ins"
  (layout and search path, source/compiled forms, registration, options,
  activation, the hook catalogue with each hook's kind, arguments and call
  site, error handling, the =alfe.plugin= API) and a rewritten "EPURE"
  section (the plug-in's behaviour per backend and OS, replacing the
  description of the bash wrapper) plus a new "EPUREE" section. The old
  =--epure= row of the option/env tables becomes a plug-in row.
- =documentation/alfe-user-manual.org=: a "Plug-ins" chapter (what they
  are, where to install one, =--list-plugins=, =--plugin=, =--plugin-path=,
  =--no-plugins=, =--compile-plugin=, =$ALFE_PLUGIN_PATH=, =$ALFE_PLUGINS=,
  =$ALFE_NO_PLUGINS=), the EPURE and EPUREE plug-ins with every option and
  environment variable, a "writing a plug-in" tutorial.
- =documentation/man/alfe.1=: OPTIONS and ENVIRONMENT entries, a short
  PLUG-INS section.
- =RELEASE_NOTES.org=: one 1–3 line entry under alfe.
- =--help= text (=*usage-banner*=) and the man page stay one vocabulary.

* Acceptance criteria

- Every option, environment variable, file and directory the plug-in
  system reads or writes is mentioned in the user manual
  (=make check-user-visible-documentation=).
- Every option the spec names is covered by a scenario
  (=make check-spec-coverage=) — satisfied together with
  =alfe-plugin-options= / =alfe-plugin-loader= (the scenarios land with the
  code; the docs land first).
- The spec's EPURE section no longer claims behaviour alfe does not have,
  and says what has *not* been validated on real CADs.

* Resolved (alfe 2.2.76)

Spec: chapters "Plug-ins", "EPURE" (rewritten, with what is NOT validated on
real CADs) and "EPUREE" in =documentation/alfe--specifications.org=, plus the
env table rows and the legacy VBScript listing now showing the two plug-in
slots. User manual: chapter "Plug-ins" (roots, source/compiled, activation,
EPURE, EPUREE, "Writing a plug-in"), the =--epure= rows fixed, environment
variables, troubleshooting, =--print-command='s =cd DIR &&=. Man page:
OPTIONS / ENVIRONMENT / PLUG-INS. =RELEASE_NOTES.org=: one entry.
=make check-spec-coverage= (44/44) and =make check-user-visible-documentation=
green. The user manual and man page were drafted from the spec by a separate
agent and reconciled with the code afterwards (source-tree root, the exact
refusal message, =$ALFE_PLUGINS= unknown names, the =cd= prefix).
